This package provides GPU accelerated versions of various LAMMPS styles.

The LAMMPS manual gives details of what hardware and CUDA software is
required on your system, and full details on how to build and use this
package.  The KOKKOS package also has GPU-enabled styles.

This package uses a library with the GPU kernels provided in lib/gpu,
which is compiled automatically by CMake as part of the LAMMPS build.
See the lib/gpu/README file and the LAMMPS manual for information on
building LAMMPS with this package.

The GPU package and its associated library was created by Mike Brown
while at Sandia and ORNL, and by Trung Nguyen while at ORNL, and
is currently maintained by Trung Nguyen at U Chicago.
